{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:StochasticMechanics.ClassicalLimitObstruction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"StochasticMechanics.ClassicalLimitObstruction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Defs"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ClassicalLimitObstruction.substrate_nontrivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ClassicalLimitObstruction.substrate_nontrivial","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/classical-limit-obstruction.lean#L54-L54","doc":"The substrate class is non-trivial (q ≠ 1 is essential). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ClassicalLimitObstruction.substrate_class","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ClassicalLimitObstruction.substrate_class","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/classical-limit-obstruction.lean#L52-L52","doc":"The obstruction class of the substrate parameter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ClassicalLimitObstruction.extends_iff_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ClassicalLimitObstruction.extends_iff_zero","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/classical-limit-obstruction.lean#L49-L49","doc":"A deformation extends iff its obstruction class vanishes.\nThis is the content of the Hochschild deformation theorem. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ClassicalLimitObstruction.deformation_extends","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ClassicalLimitObstruction.deformation_extends","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/classical-limit-obstruction.lean#L45-L45","doc":"Predicate: a deformation with obstruction class `obs` extends\nacross the classical limit q → 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ClassicalLimitObstruction.addGroupInst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ClassicalLimitObstruction.addGroupInst","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/classical-limit-obstruction.lean#L42-L42","doc":"The obstruction group has an additive group structure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ClassicalLimitObstruction.carrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ClassicalLimitObstruction.carrier","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/classical-limit-obstruction.lean#L40-L40","doc":"The underlying type of the obstruction group HH²(𝒰_q, Ad). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ClassicalLimitObstruction.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ClassicalLimitObstruction.mk","kind":"ctor","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/classical-limit-obstruction.lean#L38-L38","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ClassicalLimitObstruction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ClassicalLimitObstruction","kind":"structure","line":21,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/classical-limit-obstruction.lean#L21-L54","doc":"**Classical limit obstruction**: the Hochschild cohomology group\n`HH²(𝒰_q(𝔤), Ad)` that controls whether algebraic properties\nof the quantum universe persist through the classical limit q → 1.\n\nElements of Obs are obstructions to extending second-order\ndeformations of the Frobenius–Hopf algebra A_q across q = 1.\n\nThe Hochschild tower:\n- HH⁰(Ad): G-invariant adjoint vectors (hidden symmetries)\n- HH¹(Ad): outer derivations (infinitesimal deformations)\n- HH²(Ad): obstructions to extending deformations across q = 1\n- HH³(Ad): secondary obstructions (Massey products)\n\nA property 𝒫(q) that holds for generic non-torsion q persists\nthrough q = 1 iff its obstruction class [𝒫] ∈ HH²(Ad) vanishes. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:classical-limit-obstruction","label":"def:classical-limit-obstruction","md":"quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/classical-limit-obstruction.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}